cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AmpliTrim, please cite it as below."
title: "AmpliTrim: choosing DADA2 truncation lengths from the reads themselves"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/paytonyau/amplitrim"
abstract: >-
  AmpliTrim recommends DADA2 truncLenF and truncLenR for paired-end amplicon reads and tests candidate settings on the user's own reads: it replicates DADA2's
  quality filter from the quality scores, sets a coverage floor from the amplicon lengths, and estimates the merge yield with vsearch.
authors:
  - family-names: "Yau"
    given-names: "Payton (Tung On)"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3283-0370"
keywords:
  - DADA2
  - amplicon sequencing
  - 16S rRNA
  - ITS
  - paired-end reads
# add when releasing: date-released, and doi (from the archived release)
